    "chunk_text": "(m)cooperate with and participate in internationalorganizations, including public internationalfinancial institutions, and cooperate with domesticand foreign public institutions, concerning mattersrelated to its objects;\n\n(n)promote the financial inclusion in Sri Lanka;\n\n(p)hold, sell and dispose property, both movable andimmovable, and to enter into contracts;\n\n(q)acquire and hold such assets and incur suchliabilities as it may deem necessary; and\n\n5Central Bank of Sri Lanka\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(r)generally, do all such acts and things as arenecessary for or incidental or conducive to thecarrying out or attainment of the objects of theCentral Bank.\n\n(2) The Governing Board, Monetary Policy Board andExecutive Board shall, for the purpose of achieving theobjects of the Central Bank, exercise, discharge and performthe powers, functions and duties conferred on, or assignedto, or imposed on, the Central Bank by this Act or any otherwritten law.\n\nPART II\n\nGOVERNING BOARD, MONETARY POLICY BOARD ANDEXECUTIVE BOARD\n\n8.(1) There shall be established a Governing Board ofthe Central Bank (in this Act referred to as the \u201cGoverningBoard\u201d) which is charged with the responsibility ofoverseeing the administration and management of the affairsof the Central Bank and the determination of general policyof the Central Bank other than the monetary policy.\n\n(2) The Governing Board shall consist of the followingmembers:\u2013\n\n(a)the Secretary to the Treasury;\n\n(b)the Governor of the Central Bank who shall be theChairperson of the Governing Board; and\n\n(c)three members who shall have expertise ineconomics, banking, finance, accounting andauditing, law or risk management.\n\n(3) The Secretary to the Governing Board who shall be anemployee of the Central Bank shall be nominated by theExecutive Board.\n\nGoverningBoard of theCentral Bank.\n\n30\n\n6Central Bank of Sri Lanka\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25"
