    "chunk_text": "38.(1) Where any financial institution, which is liableto pay the levy under this Part fails to pay the levy as providedfor in section 36, such financial institution shall be deemedto be a defaulter under this Act.\n\nExemptionfrom theLevy.\n\nDefault inpayment ofthe Levy.\n\n16Finance\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n39.In this Part of this Act, unless the context otherwiserequires\u2014\n\n\u201cCommissioner-General\u201d means the Commissioner-General of Inalnd Revenue appointed or deemed tobe appointed under the Inland Revenue Act, No. 24of 2017;\n\n\u201cfinancial institution\u201dmeans\u2014\n\n(a)a licenced commercial bank or a licencedspecialized bank within the meaning of theBanking Act, No. 30 of 1988;\n\n(b)a finance company registered under theFinance Companies Act, No. 78 of 1988.\n\nPART XI\n\nCARBON TAX\n\n40.(1) There shall be levied for every year commencingfrom the date of commencement of this Act, from theregistered owner of every motor vehicle specified in theThird Schedule hereto, a tax to be called the \u201cCarbon Tax\u201d(hereinafter in this Part referred to as \u201cthe tax\u201d) at such ratesas may by specified in that Schedule.\n\n(2) The tax imposed under subsection (1) shall not applyfor any electric vehicle.\n\n41. (1) The registered owner of any relevant vehicleshall pay the tax for every year other than for the first year ofregistration of such motor vehicle to the Divisional Secretary,on or before the due date of renewal of annual registration.\n\n(2) Every Divisional Secretary who collects any amonutin accordance with the provisions of subsection (1) shallduly acknowledge the receipt of the tax so collected andremit such amount to the Commissioner-General, in suchmanner as may be prescribed.\n\nInterpretation.\n\nImposition ofCarbon Tax.\n\nRegisteredowner to paythe tax.\n\n30\n\n17Finance\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(3) The provisions which may be necessary for theimplementation of the provisions of this Part and collectionof the tax shall be prescribed by regulations made under thisAct."
